# Ciphertext file -> owner:group:mode[:format] of the decrypted file in /run.
# One line per ciphertext under /var/lib/smortress/secrets, which is root-only,
# survives every image (bootc never reconciles /var) and is where a rotation is
# written. The image's own ciphertext is only the seed for a host that has none;
# see scripts/smortress-secrets-seed.sh. scripts/sops-decrypt.sh fails closed on
# a missing ciphertext, an unlisted ciphertext, or a bad mode.
#
# This file is image-owned. It holds metadata -- a name, an owner, a mode -- and
# no secret, so the image is the only writer that matters: a new line ships with
# the build and reaches the host at the next boot. It is NOT under /etc, because
# bootc merges /etc once per deployment and keeps what the host already had, so
# a line added by a later image never arrived and every consumer failed "the
# ciphertext set and manifest disagree" until an operator fixed /etc by hand.
# The seed copies this file over /etc/smortress/secrets.manifest on every run,
# which is what sops-decrypt reads, so a host edit there is neither needed nor
# kept.
#
# format is optional:
#   yaml   the decrypted YAML is written verbatim (default)
#   value  the file's single top-level scalar is written, nothing else; a
#          restic --password-file cannot read a YAML document with a key
#
# healthchecks.yaml holds the single ping URL the freshness verifier uses; the
# whole YAML document is decryptable but only that one key is ever read.
#
# The two application secrets are single scalars because Podman secrets and the
# Immich `_FILE` variables need the bare value, not a YAML key. They stay
# root-only on purpose: smortress-app-secrets.service reads them as root and
# hands the value to each container at its own uid and mode.
# name                        uid   gid   mode  format
canary.yaml                   root  root  0400
restic-password.yaml          root  root  0400  value
r2-credentials.yaml           root  root  0400
healthchecks.yaml             root  root  0400
# The Tailscale auth key (design #767): a pre-signed, single-use key minted in
# the admin console, encrypted to the host identity. smortress-tailscale-up.service
# reads `authkey:` from it and skips enrollment when it is absent, so this line
# and its ciphertext have to land together.
tailscale.yaml                root  root  0400  yaml
immich-db-password.yaml       root  root  0400  value
opdshelf-admin-password.yaml  root  root  0400  value
# The two gateway API keys are self-issued (openssl rand -hex 32) and revocable;
# smortress-agent-config.service turns each into API_SERVER_KEY in the runtime's
# own .env, because the runtime has no _FILE variant. The hosted provider key is
# read only by agent-proxy, as a file, and is never placed in an environment: its
# ciphertext ships seeded with a random value and must be replaced with the
# provider's key before the general side can reach the provider (an unreplaced
# seed answers 401 there and nowhere else).
agent-local-api-key.yaml      root  root  0400  value
agent-general-api-key.yaml    root  root  0400  value
agent-hosted-key.yaml         root  root  0400  value
# The two facade tokens are the identity a facade process checks before it reads
# a request body: one deployment, one token, so the token is also the answer to
# "which deployment is this". Both are self-issued (openssl rand -hex 32) and
# revocable, and each gateway gets its deployment's token through its seeded
# config.yaml (rotation: docs/manual-steps.md section 40.11), so the facade is the
# only container that mounts the file.
agent-facade-personal-token.yaml root root 0400 value
agent-facade-general-token.yaml  root root 0400 value
# One password gate per web UI, not one shared string: the two UIs are separate
# authority domains, and a leak on one must not open the other. Both are
# self-issued (openssl rand -hex 32) and revocable. smortress-agent-config.service
# writes each value into its deployment's webui.env, which is where the UI reads
# it: the process has no _FILE variant, and Podman's type=env secret would carry
# the ciphertext's trailing newline into a comparison that then never matches.
agent-ui-personal-password.yaml  root root 0400 value
agent-ui-general-password.yaml   root root 0400 value
# The SimpleFIN access URL, the one credential the finance collector uses. It is
# seeded with a random value and must be replaced with a claimed one before the
# collector can read anything (an unclaimed value fails at the first request and
# publishes nothing). It reaches only smortress-agent-collect-finance.service, as
# a Podman secret at uid 1000 mode 0400: the gateway, the facades and both UIs
# never see it.
simplefin-access-url.yaml     root  root  0400  value
# The mail collector's bridge password: TutaBridge generates it on first `init`
# and prints it with `tutabridge password`. Seeded with a random value, so an
# unreplaced seed fails to authenticate and publishes nothing rather than
# appearing to work (docs/manual-steps.md section 40.15). It reaches only
# smortress-agent-collect-mail.service, as a Podman secret at uid 1000 mode 0400;
# no deployment, facade or UI ever sees it, and the Tuta account password is not
# in this repository at all.
tmail-bridge-password.yaml    root  root  0400  value
# The Brave Sync seed: the OSCrypt blob one desktop profile's join wrote, in the
# contract form `v10<base64>` that every tool here speaks. It is the chain's key --
# anything holding it can read and write the synced history -- so it reaches only
# smortress-agent-brave-seed.service, as a Podman secret at uid 1000 mode 0400, and
# that unit plants it into the browsing profile's Preferences (0600). Seeded with a
# random 32-byte hex placeholder that is deliberately not a v10 blob: the seeder
# refuses it, so an unreplaced seed is a failed unit naming the missing step rather
# than a browser that silently syncs nothing (docs/manual-steps.md section 40.17).
brave-sync-seed.yaml          root  root  0400  value
# The smores account's password hash. It is consumed twice: the install renders it
# into Ignition (scripts/render-ignition.sh) and the boot unit
# smortress-password.service re-applies it through chpasswd -e, because bootc never
# reconciles /var -- without the unit, /etc/shadow would stay whatever the install
# left there and a reinstall would need the operator to carry the hash. `value`
# because chpasswd -e takes the bare hash: a field holding `hash: $6$...` is a
# password nobody can type.
smores-password-hash.yaml        root root 0400 value
# The deploy receiver's HMAC key (design #798). Two single scalars, and the
# listener accepts either: `webhook-secret` is what a CI job signs with today and
# `webhook-secret-next` is the rotation slot, shipped with a random 32-byte hex
# value nobody holds, so it accepts nothing until it is replaced. Rotation is
# therefore add next -> deploy -> swap -> deploy -> remove, which fits inside one
# platform deploy and a reboot without a window where the old secret is refused.
# The listener refuses to start when the current file is empty or missing -- a
# failed decrypt is then a unit that never answers the tailnet rather than one that
# accepts unsigned requests -- and the next file only widens the window when it is
# present and non-empty. `value` because the listener compares the raw scalar: a
# file holding only `webhook-secret: <hex>` would compare against a key name.
webhook-secret.yaml           root  root  0400  value
webhook-secret-next.yaml      root  root  0400  value
# The one Healthchecks check the receiver owns (`deploy`). Its URL is the
# capability to keep that check green, so it is read from this file by
# deploy_notify and by the heartbeat, never echoed, journaled or passed in argv.
# `value` so the heartbeat hands the bare URL to curl, with no YAML parsing
# between a capability and the request that spends it.
deploy-ping-url.yaml          root  root  0400  value
# Agent-only (docs/agent-identity.md): the general agent's GitHub identities, read
# by the shell dispatcher and handed to one general job. `value` because the job
# reads the file's bytes as GH_TOKEN; no other process on the host reads them.
agent-github-token.yaml       root  root  0400  value
sdlc-github-token.yaml        root  root  0400  value
